\f0\fs32 \cf2 Clinic Patient Portal\

\fs28 1. Context\

\fs24 A. What is this project\
about? This project is a UX redesign of an\
OB-GYN clinic\'92s website and\
patient portal.\
B. Why did I choose it? \
1. Personal Connection\
This redesign is inspired by my own experience as a patient at this clinic. I noticed the existing portal was difficult to use, and I wanted to explore how UX design could improve a real-world healthcare experience.\
2. Industry Relevance\
The healthcare industry is a major sector in New York City and continues to grow regardless of economic shifts. I\'92m interested in working in this space because it combines complex systems with meaningful impact on people\'92s lives.\
3. Accessibility Focus\
Accessibility in digital products is something I\'92m personally passionate about and often see overlooked in design. This project allowed me to apply accessibility best practices to make the portal more inclusive for all patients.\

\fs28 2. Sitemap\

\fs24 A. This sitemap visualizes the information\
architecture of the redesigned OB-GYN clinic website and its patient portal. It maps how users navigate from the public-facing homepage into the secure portal, and how key sections within the portal are organized for better accessibility, clarity, and ease of use.\

\fs28 3. Wireframes\

\fs24 A. Low Fidelity: Early sketch exploring the clinic\'92s homepage layout and content hierarchy.\
B. Mid Fidelity: This is a mid-fidelity wireframe of the patient clinic website homepage, sign-up page, and patient portal dashboard.\
C. High Fidelity: This is an image of a high-fidelity wireframe of the patient clinic website homepage.\

